intent: merge the R=10,000 admission-cost tier into results/micro/b10_assurance_scaling.json for a real 3-point (100/1,000/10,000) scaling fit, and rewrite F2/F2b in the findings doc honestly: admission stays sub-linear over the full 100x range (~15x cost for 100x repo growth) but the growth rate itself worsens at the second decade (6.3x-7.0x per D vs 2.2x-2.3x in the first decade); the more durable finding is that admission's relative cheapness vs evidence checking widens with scale (3.6x -> 6.1x -> 12.75x), not that admission itself stays flat
